# Katana sample drawing - a small site plan.
# Run:  katana_cli samples/site_plan.kcs
# or open the saved project from the GUI: File > Open -> samples/site_plan

# ---- layers -------------------------------------------------------------
LAYER NEW BOUNDARY #FFD54F
LAYER NEW BUILDING #4FC3F7
LAYER NEW ROAD     #9E9E9E
LAYER NEW UTILITY  #E040FB
LAYER NEW ANNOT    #FFFFFF
LAYER NEW DIMS     #81C784

# ---- parcel boundary ----------------------------------------------------
LAYER SET BOUNDARY
PLINE 0,0 160,0 175,90 80,130 0,100 CLOSE

# ---- building footprint -------------------------------------------------
LAYER SET BUILDING
RECT 40,35 110,85
# a bay window off the south wall
PLINE 60,35 60,25 85,25 85,35

# ---- road ---------------------------------------------------------------
LAYER SET ROAD
# centreline: straight run into a curve at the east end
LINE 5,15 120,15
ARC 120,15 145,18 160,32
# kerb lines, offset both sides of the straight
LINE 5,20 120,20
LINE 5,10 120,10

# ---- utilities ----------------------------------------------------------
LAYER SET UTILITY
LINE 20,60 20,15
LINE 20,60 75,60
CIRCLE 20,60 2.5
CIRCLE 20,15 2.5
CIRCLE 75,60 2.5

# ---- annotation ---------------------------------------------------------
LAYER SET ANNOT
TEXT 52,58 7 "BUILDING A"
TEXT 6,112 6 "PARCEL 42"
TEXT 30,7 4 "ACCESS ROAD"
TEXT 24,64 3 "MH-01"

# ---- dimensions ---------------------------------------------------------
LAYER SET DIMS
DIM 0,0 160,0 -14
DIM 40,35 110,35 -6
DIM 0,0 0,100 -14

# ---- hatching -----------------------------------------------------------
# Angles in degrees, spacing in MODEL units - so the pattern keeps its size on
# the ground as the view zooms, which is the point of a hatch on a survey
# drawing. Zoom out far enough and it is drawn as a solid tone instead, because
# lines closer together than about three pixels cannot be told apart anyway.
HATCH NEW brick 0 0.6 90 0.6
HATCH NEW hardstanding 45 1.5
LAYER HATCH BUILDING brick

# ---- alignment ----------------------------------------------------------
# The access road centreline, defined by its PIs. PI 1 is rounded with R = 40
# and 10 m spirals either side; the tangents, spirals and arc are derived, so
# moving a PI recomputes the corner. Drawn as the amber overlay with its key
# stations; Terrain > Cut Section Along Alignment... cuts a section down it.
ALIGN NEW access 0,-30 60,-30 160,20
ALIGN SET access 1 40 10 10
# Its design grade line: a sag of 40 m at chainage 80. Cut Section Along
# Alignment... then shows the design against the ground, with its low point.
ALIGN DESIGN access 0,52 80,50.5,40 171,53

LAYER SET BOUNDARY
LIST
